WEBVTT

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.830
The Imber is shifting to
Tragheit Brecher configuration.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.330
Inertial controller output is increasing.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.620
Calculations for all trajectories is complete.
Target Drop will be reached in five...

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.500
Four, three, two, one.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.330
Impact confirmed.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.790
The target has completely stopped.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.790
Target Drop is crossing
pressure resistance levels.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.040
Target destruction is confirmed.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.910
That's a wrap.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.160
Yukiho.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.790
Y-yes! Haruka, good work.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.370
That's a wrap. Please begin
preparations to return.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.450
Thank you, Yukiho.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.330
Visibility's really good today.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:59.370
Look. That's where you came to get me
last time, Imber. My hometown.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.790
It's so pretty...

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.160
Do you remember, Imber?

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:10.370
We were both there, weren't we?
I was SO happy.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.950
I got a flower, too.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:19.500
Someday, I want you to show me
YOUR hometown, Imber. Ha!

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.870
S.O.S. kikoeta

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:31.830
Yatto anata ni kikoeta?

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.790
Kakko kawaiku ne

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.330
Fujun, junsui, dotchi no character?

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:54.160
Onaji na no kashira

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.700
Love beat ga sokudo zenkai

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.700
Kizuita, kore wa tokubetsu na mission... Wakatta

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:08.120
Honki misechau yo, kanaechau kara

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:12.000
Sora o tsukinuketa sekai de

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:18.950
Fushigi na omoi kanjita yo, shunkan de suki!

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.000
Egao de katsu desho, yappa egao wa tadashii no

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.330
Egao de katsu desho, yappa egao wa tadashii no

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:32.910
Naiteta chiisa na watashi ga tachimukau

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.250
Nandaro doki doki, chotto teate ga hitsuyou ne

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.540
Nandaro doki doki, chotto teate ga hitsuyou ne

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:46.620
Binetsu na kibun wa anata no sei kamo, S.O.S.!

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.620
Konpeito Night Talks

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.000
Huh?

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.120
A-a field trip to the beach?!

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:07.790
Yes. It was on short notice, and came up
very fast. The school is all but empty today.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.450
Jeez. Ain't that a beast.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.620
I was suddenly able to get a day off, so
I thought I'd come give Haruka a surprise.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.950
I even got this costume ready.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.580
Still...
Still...

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.540
It's quite hot, isn't it?

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.450
Yes, it's hot, isn't it?

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.660
The beach, huh? Must be nice...

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.450
The beach!

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.250
It's the beach, isn't it?

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:38.950
We're really here, right?
A beach in the south!

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:43.580
Of course we are. If this isn't a southern
beach, just where would we be?

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.540
I know, right?

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:50.250
I really wish this were a field trip
to the beach, though...

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.410
Yeah, right? This is still work, right?

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.910
Of course it is.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:55.830
But...

00:03:55.830 --> 00:04:00.450
For us to come out HERE just to do
activation tests for Imber and the others...

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.450
You really don't know anything, do you?

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.910
We have installations out here,

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.290
so it's ideal for us to conduct actual
maneuvers and pilot training.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.330
Huh.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:14.540
In any case, Imber's and Nebula's parts
were developed in this factory.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.500
Wait, so does that mean
that Imber was born here?

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.580
Huh? Of course it doesn't mean that.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:23.700
Then...

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.120
Let's put aside difficult
conversations for the moment.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.120
Today is to reward those who, every day,

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.620
perform the difficult task
of destroying Drops.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:38.200
Now then, all who are not busy,
please enjoy the beach.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.410
All right, the beach is calling you.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.790
And work is calling YOU, sir.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:49.790
Fine.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.250
Huh? Imber...

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.410
He's undergoing thorough maintenance
to prepare for tomorrow's testing.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.120
Oh, really?

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.750
Say, Haruka, what's your favorite color?

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.000
Favorite... color?

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.750
Um, it'd have to be pink, I guess.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.750
Pink, huh? Okay, leave it to me.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:16.950
Huh?

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:21.120
Hyaaa! I got me a fish!

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.080
I'm counting on you for dinner...

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:24.580
It's fish season!
I'm counting on you for dinner...

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:25.700
It's fish season!
Sorewa!

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:29.330
So, hyaa!

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.580
Good luck!

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:45.040
This feels great! Right, Idiot Ribbon?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:51.290
I got a sea cucumber! Maybe this'll be
a good souvenir for Yayoi!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.040
Why, you...

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.540
We've come to the beach,
so why aren't you swimming?!

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.450
Why'd you wear something like that?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.790
Uh, well, this swimsuit
is kind of embarrassing...

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.290
What's this?
Shall I expose you to everyone?

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.160
Let go! Let go!

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.290
I'm sorry.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.250
It took me a while to change.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.620
Is something the matter?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.160
Th-these are...

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.660
WHOA!

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.290
Is there something on me?

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.080
Yeah, sure are.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.830
Like gangbusters.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.580
Not yet! I haven't lost yet!
The challenge is yet to come!

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:43.080
Don't sleep while someone else is talking!

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:47.000
What's that?

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:48.790
There they go.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.250
What is that?

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:55.330
Huh? They're doing ignition testing
of the iDOLs' new nozzle.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.700
This is the only place they could
open it up full throttle.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.250
What an incredible sound...

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.290
It rumbles in your stomach, huh?

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.660
Yeah.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:10.580
Still, if all that fire comes out,
won't Imber get hot?

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:12.040
Huh?

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.080
Haruka...

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.790
You're an idiot, aren't you? The nozzle's
fitted on the bottom of the iDOLs' feet.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.080
There's no way
it'd be hot or anything, would it?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.200
Yeah, but still!

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.040
Come on. Forget about that and let's swim.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.540
Haruka?

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:36.700
I'm gonna go see how Imber's doing.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.160
Jeez. She's an iDOL-loving fool.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:47.750
All right! All right!

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.040
Over there. Be careful.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.950
Take it slowly. Slowly!

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:54.830
Once you're done here,
do a final check of the drive systems.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.000
Understood!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:02.290
There's still plenty left on the checklist.
Hang in there.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.700
Ma'am.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.080
There's so much smoke!

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:39.080
Be more careful over there.
We can't go hurting the Imber's feelings!

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:39.830
No. 7 Frame G stress gauge is stable from 35 to 38.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.580
Cables 1 through 5 released.
No. 7 Frame G stress gauge is stable from 35 to 38.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.870
No. 7 Frame G stress gauge is stable from 35 to 38.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:48.200
Version updates for organic device polymerase
will now be carried out in Block 9.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.540
Please confirm your biochemical
databases have been updated.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:55.700
No. 4 Area, Section B
is currently a zero-G zone.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.160
Some coolant over here, please!
No. 4 Area, Section B
is currently a zero-G zone.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.910
Chief, I'm sending the status
of the Tragheit Brecher module.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:08.200
Line 1 is blue. Line 3 is green.
Line 7 is yellow.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:11.200
Im...ber?
Message to all staff: Level 2 electrical field
correction will begin in 20 minutes.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.330
Message to all staff: Level 2 electrical field
correction will begin in 20 minutes.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.580
Surprised?
Message to all staff: Level 2 electrical field
correction will begin in 20 minutes.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:14.790
An alarm will sound three minutes prior.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.040
Ma'am.
An alarm will sound three minutes prior.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.410
This is your first time, isn't it?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.200
That is the Imber's core.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.160
Core?

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:28.580
Yes. The real Imber lives...
Rather, is in there.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:34.040
The real... Imber?

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:37.450
What a haul!

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.450
I ain't done yet! Not yet, not yet!

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.870
He sure is happy.

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.700
Anyway, Haruka sure is taking her time.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:45.910
Yes, she is.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:48.200
Just forget about that Idiot Ribbon.

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:51.580
Jeez. All she does is make us worry.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.290
107 years ago, the moon's
destruction brought about

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:06.500
the greatest calamity in history,

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:11.500
one that threatened humanity's
existence: Lost Artemis.

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:23.750
That unprecedented crisis
also presented mankind with a gift...

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:34.410
A complex silicon structure never before
seen. It is what he now call the iDOLs.

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.750
Huh? Then...

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:41.540
Yes. To be precise, we humans
didn't create the iDOLs.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:49.040
They were discovered in craters,
possessing almost limitless energy.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:56.040
Our research continued, and two geniuses
succeeded in analyzing the structures.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.790
And they were named "iDOLs."

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.080
Research progressed further,

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:07.040
and finally the humanoid interface
called Prometheus was born.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:12.080
The Imber was the first of these.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:18.370
Over here too, please.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:18.870
Ma'am.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:29.870
Finished!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:37.750
Say, Chihaya, how's this? This is WAY more
cool, right? I've come up with a name, too.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.830
Okay? He's called "Epi"!

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.290
Hey! Darn it, Chihaya!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:47.290
Jeez, I'm so depressed!

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:53.500
Development of the iDOLs
went well for the most part.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.870
But there was just one problem.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:00.910
For some reason,
they only respond to females.

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:04.620
What's more, only select
few can pilot them.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.580
It's as if they're being picky...

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:12.660
The iDOLs only like pretty girls?
That means...

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.660
For the moment, this is everything
we know about the iDOLs.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:21.500
Rather, everything I've just told you
is conjecture based on our tests,

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:22.410
nothing more.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:27.000
We don't know what the iDOLs
are really thinking.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.000
Or if they have minds capable of reasoning.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.830
We don't know even that.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:37.870
But, Imber has a mind.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.870
Is that really so?

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:44.080
The humanlike reactions
the iDOLs have shown

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.290
may simply be mechanical,
reflexive actions.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:52.660
We might just be interpreting that
as them having a mind.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.200
B-but!

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.620
According to data learned
by analyzing the core,

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.660
it seems there are a total of five of them.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:04.000
But even if we find the remaining two,
how much closer could we get to the truth?

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:11.040
We have no means up letting us determine
whether it's really the truth.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:16.120
So, can you say for sure they have minds?

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:25.450
Maybe only the iDOLs themselves
can know the truth.

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:29.200
The same way that the
human mind can't be seen...

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:32.830
Hey, Ribbon!

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.620
This way!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.660
Ritsuko...

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.660
There's something I want you to see.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.660
Well? A masterpiece, huh?

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:50.200
Um... How can I put this...

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.750
Nice color, huh?

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.160
It was a lot of work getting this color!

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:58.290
Um...

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:00.540
Whoa, the heck's with that color?

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.040
Just what is going on?

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.500
You should be worried
about your OWN color!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.250
It really is a good color, huh?

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:16.910
Hey, Yukiho! It's because you
slathered all that cream on me!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.250
Turned out nicely, didn't it?

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:22.660
The Imber's happy, too.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.250
Yeah...

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:28.080
I think so.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.540
Mondenkind
Hamlet of Relaxation

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.120
I-I can feel it!

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:43.290
Whoa, looks painful.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.000
You shouldn't have to force yourself.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:49.080
But they have a hot spring here.
What's the point if we don't use it?!

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.330
I think you're better off not forcing it.

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:53.540
That's right.
I think you're better off not forcing it.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.450
Pretty, isn't it?

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:09.450
Imber was pretty too, right?

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.120
Not really my taste, though.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.250
Iori...

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:17.500
Even if you think about hard stuff
like what the iDOLs are,

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.160
it won't get you anywhere, will it?

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.290
Imber is Imber, nothing more.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:25.950
Yeah...

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:28.120
Huh? How did you...?

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.120
It's obvious you're keeping abreast.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.120
Huh?!
It's obvious you're keeping abreast.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.250
What are you doing?

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:40.200
The boss told me about the iDOLs
when I was here before.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:47.750
Your merit is that you're foolishly optimistic.
Idiot Ribbon should act like Idiot Ribbon.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:50.830
Yeah. Thank you.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:54.200
Iori, you're so kind.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:54.830
What're you talkin' about?!

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:55.160
Aah, youth.
What're you talkin' about?!

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:55.910
Aah, youth.
I'm just passing on info as an Idolmas-

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:56.870
I'm just passing on info as an Idolmas-

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.700
Hey, Yukiho! Why're you sleeping?!

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.540
That's dangerous, Yukiho.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.040
O-owww!

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:07.200
Iori!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.580
Oh, my.
Iori!

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:15.120
Hi! Good evening, ya-yoi-yo!

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:16.950
RELAXATION

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:16.120
It's Yayoi Takatsuki's Yayoi-style Radio!

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.290
Jeez. This sunburn is REALLY burned.
It's Yayoi Takatsuki's Yayoi-style Radio!

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:20.500
RELAXATION

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.450
Iori...

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.000
Oh, where's Haruka?

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.950
She said she wanted to get some air,
so she's been up on the roof.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:31.450
They say that tonight we can see
a big Konpeito Snow!

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:38.160
Different areas are holding their own events,
so if you have a partner, tonight could be romantic!

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:42.910
If you don't have a partner, don't give up
and keep forging on ahead!

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.790
Huh? What am I talking about?

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.290
Imber is Imber, nothing more.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.040
I know, right?

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:54.540
Imber is Imber.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:58.330
Honey and
Ujina Yogurt
Diet

00:16:56.500 --> 00:17:02.000
And I... am me.

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:19.160
Okay, Imber.

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:21.910
Wanna go to the beach?

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:40.700
What is going on?

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.160
Looks like a special, late-night test.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.580
Haruka only just requested permission.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.540
A late-night date, eh?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.120
This is no small feat, is it?

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:54.290
Indeed.

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:34.870
Say, Imber...

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:42.250
I heard a lot of things about you today
from our boss, and got a little worried.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:48.250
I thought that, maybe, I really didn't
know anything about you.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.290
But...

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:58.500
That you gave me this flower, that's real,
right? And that you came for me. Right?

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:01.620
This is the real you, right?

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.370
I don't know what you've done up till now,

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:09.500
but I want to get to know
who you are going forward.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:12.830
I want to know more about you!

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:18.370
So, first, I want you
to know more about me.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:24.870
Ta-daa! Silly, huh? We match.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:29.910
This kind of thing is embarrassing,
so I haven't shown anyone.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.450
You're the first one, Imber.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.120
So, once again...

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:43.830
I'm Haruka Amami. Born April 3, '91. I'm 16.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.950
I'm from Taketori-cho.
You went there not long ago, right?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:51.620
My family is my grandpa and my brother.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:55.750
My favorite things are
corn dogs and penguins.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:57.500
Also...

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.330
Unusual, isn't it?

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.830
For us to see such a large-scale
Konpeito Snow.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:23.500
An ultra-small-sized meteor shower
making contact with the atmosphere...

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:32.080
Proof that upheaval has occurred in the
orbital ring that we call konpeito, is that it?

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:36.080
Though that is a tactless way of putting it.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:50.330
Still, it's precisely because
it's being destroyed

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:53.330
that the world is this beautiful, isn't it?

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:58.540
So pretty...

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:05.330
Say, Imber, did you really
come from out there?

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.290
Oh.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:18.540
I want to know more, MORE about you.

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:24.000
So stick with me, okay? Imber.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:35.370
Toki o wataru seija no you ni

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:44.330
Donna kodoku ni naite ita no?

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:53.200
Haruka tooi hoshi o tsunagi

00:21:53.200 --> 00:22:01.750
Ne, omoi o egaku wa, sora o miagete

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:13.200
Dear boy, itsumo kokoro ni anata o sagaseba

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:22.160
Ah, dakishimeru hodo ni tsuyoi hikari o hanatsu no

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:31.120
Mabataku kidou ga futari no mejirushi

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:42.750
Ima doko de mite ite mo truth kanjitete

00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:57.450
Okay, for the take!

00:22:57.450 --> 00:22:58.330
We're good here, too.

00:22:58.330 --> 00:22:59.540
Clear the way!

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:00.750
Okay, here goes.

00:23:01.370 --> 00:23:03.330
Hrm. Yup. Yeah, yeah!

00:23:04.370 --> 00:23:05.620
Oh, that's nice!

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:06.950
Good, WAY good!

00:23:06.950 --> 00:23:10.040
Ha. I got me the mother lode.
Good, WAY good!

00:23:10.540 --> 00:23:12.000
Ooh, that's nice!

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:13.080
Huh?

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:15.330
You just let Naraba be?

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:19.120
If he goes to the beach,
he won't come back for a week.

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:21.750
Oh, ma'am, this is for you.

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:24.330
It's sea cucumber extract,
good for small wrinkles!

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:26.040
Hoh-hoh.

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:41.080
Preview
Keyboard

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:28.660
Let's try saying our favorite mottos.

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:31.750
Always have presence of mind.

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:34.120
Exertion wins over genius.

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:37.160
Xanthid crab.
